# Home Assistant services

## Gate

Load only when the user authorized Home Assistant **and** used an explicit
mutate verb this turn (**turn on/off**, **call**, **set**, **unlock**,
**disarm**, **delete**, **reload**, **restart**) naming the entity or
object. Otherwise stay on `home-assistant-entities`. Always pair with
`home-assistant-safety` before any service call.

No Home Assistant MCP discovered — use REST/WebSocket API only. **Do not
invent MCP tool names.**

## Inventory before mutate

1. Resolve `entity_id` from `GET /api/states` or user paste this turn
   (`home-assistant-entities`).
2. Prefer `GET /api/services` to confirm domain/service exists before calling.
3. State planned domain/service + entity_id in one line; then call.

## Live API mutate map

| Action | Endpoint | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Call service | `POST /api/services/<domain>/<service>` | body: `{"entity_id": "...", ...}` |
| Fire event | `POST /api/events/<event_type>` | only when user named the event |
| Template render (read-ish) | `POST /api/template` | no secrets in templates echoed |

Common domains (examples — resolve from `/api/services`, do not invent):

- `homeassistant.turn_on` / `turn_off` / `toggle`
- `light.turn_on` / `light.turn_off`
- `switch.turn_on` / `switch.turn_off`
- `climate.set_temperature`
- `lock.unlock` / `lock.lock` — **high risk**
- `alarm_control_panel.alarm_disarm` — **high risk**
- `cover.open_cover` / `close_cover` — garage-shaped risk

Automation / script hygiene (when API or UI exposes it):

- Prefer disable/pause over delete when silence is enough
- Delete automation/script only with explicit **delete** + object name
- Restart / reload all YAML only when user explicitly asked

## Defaults

- Prefer the narrowest service targeting a single named `entity_id`.
- Prefer `turn_off` / pause over restarting Home Assistant.
- Never bulk-act across unrelated domains without listed entity_ids.
- State which service + data fields you used in the receipt.

## High-risk services

Before unlock, disarm, garage open, or HVAC setpoint changes: restate the
entity_id and effect; require the explicit verb this turn naming that entity.

## Operator receipt (mutate)

- domain.service
- entity_id(s)
- key data fields (no tokens)
- resulting state from follow-up `GET /api/states/<entity_id>` when useful

## Related (this plugin)

- `home-assistant-entities` — list/get before mutate
- `home-assistant-safety` — gates and token refuse
